THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

The MIT license above covers the DroidVM source code (Kotlin sources, resources,
build scripts and tools). The APK and app/src/main/jniLibs + assets/qemu also
contain third-party software distributed under their own licenses:

  * QEMU 11.1.3 (qemu-system-x86_64, qemu-system-aarch64, qemu-img)
    GPL-2.0-only (parts GPL-2.0-or-later, LGPL, BSD, MIT)
    https://www.qemu.org  source: https://gitlab.com/qemu-project/qemu
  * Android builds of QEMU and its libraries from the Termux project
    https://github.com/termux/termux-packages (build recipes and patches),
    https://packages.termux.dev  — glib (LGPL-2.1+), pixman (MIT), libslirp (BSD-3),
    zstd (BSD-3/GPL-2), libpng (libpng), libjpeg-turbo (BSD), gnutls (LGPL-2.1+),
    nettle (LGPL-3+/GPL-2+), and others; versions listed in assets/qemu/VERSIONS.json
  * SeaBIOS (LGPL-3.0), SeaVGABIOS (LGPL-3.0), EDK2 / OVMF / AAVMF
    (BSD-2-Clause-Patent), iPXE option ROMs (GPL-2.0)
  * AndroidX / Jetpack Compose / Material 3 / Kotlin libraries (Apache-2.0)

As required by the GPL, the corresponding source code of QEMU and the GPL/LGPL
libraries is available from the upstream projects and the Termux package
sources linked above, for the exact versions listed in VERSIONS.json.
